{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "The increment is implemented within the Spring XD 1.x code base (Java 8 / Spring Boot 1.x era); the generic Spring Framework 6 / Java 17 preamble does not apply to the XD modules referenced by the user stories (Rabbit sink, DIRT runtime, hdfs-dataset module).",
    "U1: Batching is implemented in the Rabbit sink's outbound message handler with an in-memory buffer that flushes when batchSize messages accumulate and on channel stop/drain; exposed as module options batchingEnabled (default false) and batchingSize (default 100), recorded in the module options metadata.",
    "U2: Delivered as a reusable Gradle plugin/convention script ('spring-xd-module') that declares Spring XD dependencies in a provided scope, configures the Spring Boot plugin with MODULE layout, and applies standard boilerplate (repositories, dependency management); assumes the Boot module layout scoping issue #2187 workaround available in the targeted Boot version.",
    "U3: Acceptance tests reuse the existing Spring XD acceptance test framework with an embedded/mini HDFS cluster fixture; tests cover dataset write/read, formats and rollover, and are wired as a dedicated Gradle task into the CI build.",
    "U4: Compression support refactored to a pluggable codec registry with module properties that override default codecs and allow custom codec configuration, following up on PR #1346 while keeping backward-compatible defaults.",
    "U5/U6: Benchmarks reuse the existing performance test harness against a dedicated Rabbit environment; results stored in the standard snapshot format for direct comparison with previous baselines; U6 reuses the U5 setup with compression toggled on.",
    "U7: DIRT runtime database requirement made conditional via a configuration property (e.g., xd.dirt.db.enabled=false) gating datasource/JPA/job-repository auto-configuration so admin and container nodes start and run stream processing without any database.",
    "U8: RxJava support implemented as a core adapter fulfilling the XD processor module contract, bridging an RxJava Observable chain to the module's input/output message channels, plus a base class developers extend."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single experienced developer performs all work; estimates are effort in work-hours, not elapsed calendar time.",
    "An existing Spring XD development environment, source repository, CI infrastructure, and performance benchmark harness are available and functional.",
    "The Spring Boot module layout scoping issue (spring-boot#2187) has a usable workaround in the Boot version targeted, so U2 is not blocked.",
    "RabbitMQ and HDFS test instances (embedded, fixtures, or containers) are available for integration and acceptance testing.",
    "Benchmark hardware/environment equivalent to the one used for previous performance snapshots is available, and prior snapshot data is accessible for comparison.",
    "Scope is limited to the eight user stories; no changes to public APIs beyond new module options and properties are required.",
    "Documentation effort covers module option metadata, reference documentation sections, and release notes only.",
    "Estimates represent single most likely values including developer testing; peer review is part of normal flow with rework covered by the finalization activity."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-01",
      "activity_name": "Increment analysis and design",
      "activity_description": "Analyze all eight user stories, identify affected modules (Rabbit sink, Gradle build, acceptance tests, compression, benchmarks, DIRT runtime, RxJava contract), and produce the design for each change.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-02",
      "activity_name": "U1: Implement Rabbit sink batching",
      "activity_description": "Implement buffered batch publishing in the Rabbit sink message handler with batchingEnabled and batchingSize (default 100) options, including flush on size threshold and on channel stop/drain, and register options in module metadata.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-03",
      "activity_name": "U1: Unit and integration tests for batching",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests (mocked RabbitTemplate verifying batched publishes, option validation, defaults) and an integration test of the sink against a Rabbit fixture.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-04",
      "activity_name": "U1: Document batching options",
      "activity_description": "Document batchingEnabled and batchingSize in the Rabbit sink reference documentation and option descriptions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-05",
      "activity_name": "U2: Implement Gradle module build plugin",
      "activity_description": "Create the 'spring-xd-module' Gradle plugin/convention script that declares Spring XD dependencies as provided, configures the Boot plugin for MODULE layout, and applies boilerplate build configuration.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-06",
      "activity_name": "U2: Validate plugin and document usage",
      "activity_description": "Apply the plugin to a sample module project, verify packaging and MODULE layout output, and write usage documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-07",
      "activity_name": "U3: Design hdfs-dataset acceptance scenarios",
      "activity_description": "Define acceptance test scenarios for the hdfs-dataset module (write/read round trip, supported formats, rollover) and required fixtures.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-08",
      "activity_name": "U3: Implement hdfs-dataset acceptance tests",
      "activity_description": "Implement the acceptance tests using the XD acceptance test framework with an embedded/mini HDFS cluster fixture, stream deployment, and result assertions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 20
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-09",
      "activity_name": "U3: Wire acceptance tests into CI build",
      "activity_description": "Add a dedicated Gradle task and environment configuration so the hdfs-dataset acceptance tests run as part of every CI build.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-10",
      "activity_name": "U4: Implement configurable compression support",
      "activity_description": "Refactor compression into a pluggable codec registry with properties to override default codecs and pass custom codec configuration, preserving backward-compatible defaults (follow-up to PR #1346).",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-11",
      "activity_name": "U4: Tests for compression customization",
      "activity_description": "Write unit and integration tests covering codec override, custom codec registration, and default behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-12",
      "activity_name": "U4: Document compression options",
      "activity_description": "Document the new compression customization properties and examples in the reference documentation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-13",
      "activity_name": "U5: Prepare Rabbit batching benchmark setup",
      "activity_description": "Prepare the benchmark environment and scripts/configurations for Rabbit runs with batchingEnabled=true and batchingSize=100, plus parameterized runs at varied batch sizes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-14",
      "activity_name": "U5: Execute batching benchmark runs",
      "activity_description": "Execute baseline benchmark runs with batching enabled (default size 100 and varied sizes) and collect results in the standard snapshot format.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-15",
      "activity_name": "U5: Analyze batching results and report",
      "activity_description": "Compare batching benchmark results with previous performance snapshots, record granular per-size results, and write the comparison report.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-16",
      "activity_name": "U6: Configure compression benchmark runs",
      "activity_description": "Reconfigure the benchmark harness (reusing the U5 setup) for Rabbit runs with compression enabled.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-17",
      "activity_name": "U6: Execute compression benchmark runs",
      "activity_description": "Execute baseline benchmark runs with compression enabled on Rabbit and collect results in the standard snapshot format.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-18",
      "activity_name": "U6: Analyze compression results and report",
      "activity_description": "Compare compression benchmark results with previous performance snapshots and write the comparison report.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-19",
      "activity_name": "U7: Implement optional DB requirement in DIRT",
      "activity_description": "Make datasource/JPA/job-repository auto-configuration in the DIRT runtime conditional on a property so admin and container nodes start and run stream-only processing with no database.",
      "most_likely_effort": 18
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-20",
      "activity_name": "U7: Tests for DB-disabled runtime",
      "activity_description": "Write tests verifying runtime startup without a database, stream processing correctness in DB-less mode, and unchanged behavior with the option enabled.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-21",
      "activity_name": "U7: Document DB-less setup",
      "activity_description": "Document the property and steps to run DIRT without a database for stream-processing-only deployments.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-22",
      "activity_name": "U8: Implement RxJava processor contract",
      "activity_description": "Implement the core XD processor module interface contract with an adapter bridging an RxJava Observable chain to the module's input/output message channels, plus an extendable base class.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-23",
      "activity_name": "U8: Tests and sample RxJava processor module",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for the RxJava adapter and build a sample processor module using the RxJava API to validate the contract end to end.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-24",
      "activity_name": "U8: Document RxJava processor support",
      "activity_description": "Document how to create a processor module using the RxJava API, including a code example.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-25",
      "activity_name": "Increment integration and regression testing",
      "activity_description": "Run the full build, module integration tests, and cross-feature regression (e.g., batching combined with compression on Rabbit), and confirm the CI build including new acceptance tests is green.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-26",
      "activity_name": "Review rework, release notes, and finalization",
      "activity_description": "Address code review findings, finalize release notes covering all eight user stories, and prepare the increment for merge/release.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 226
  }
}

